  "marks": "Top band (5•6 marks) Thorough discussion with developed points and clear reasoning.\nMid band (3•4 marks) Some discussion with partial development.\nLower band (1•2 marks) Limited response with basic points.\n\nIndicative content:\n• Star ratings give customers confidence about the quality of service they will receive, helping them make informed choices.\n• A higher star rating allows the hotel to charge premium prices, increasing revenue and profit margins.\n• Ratings bring media attention and prestige, which can attract more bookings and wealthier clientele.\n• However, maintaining high standards is expensive • highly trained staff, quality ingredients, and immaculate facilities are required.\n• Losing a star can damage reputation and lead to a drop in bookings."
