  "marks": "Top band (8-10): Comprehensive discussion with multiple factors linked to food safety, efficiency, and legislation.\nMid band (4-7): Good discussion of several factors with some development.\nLower band (1-3): Basic identification of factors.\nIndicative content:\n• The workflow should follow a logical sequence (delivery → storage → preparation → cooking → serving → cleaning) to prevent cross contamination.\n• Separate areas for raw and cooked food to meet food safety legislation.\n• Adequate space for large equipment (ovens, fryers, walk-in fridges) with safe access around them.\n• A staffing area with lockers and changing facilities, separate from food areas.\n• A wash area near the entrance so staff can sanitise hands before entering the kitchen.\n• The serving area (pass) should be positioned for easy access by waiting staff to minimise delays.\n• Cleaning/washing area should be away from food preparation to prevent contamination.\n• Compliance with health and safety legislation (fire exits, ventilation, non-slip flooring)."
 }
]

