+    "expect": "Top band (5-6): Thorough explanation covering multiple EHO responsibilities with clear reasoning.\nMid band (3-4): Sound explanation of at least two responsibilities.\nLower band (1-2): Basic identification with limited development.\nIndicative content:\n• The EHO inspects food businesses for hygiene, storage, equipment, and documentation standards.\n• They collect evidence (food samples, photographs, interviews) during inspections.\n• They investigate outbreaks of food poisoning to identify the source and prevent further cases.\n• They enforce environmental health laws and can prosecute businesses that break the law.\n• They award food hygiene ratings (0–5) that are displayed publicly, influencing customer choice.\n• Their role protects the public by ensuring food businesses maintain safe standards.",
