+      "truth": "FSA consumer guidance defines the danger zone as 8°C to 63°C and gives time-temperature combinations for cooking, including 70°C for 2 minutes or 75°C for 30 seconds. Option A: update every temperature reference to that guidance. Option B: retain 5°C only as a fridge operating target and distinguish it from the 8°C danger-zone threshold. This would ripple through content, conclusion, exam tip, practice material and flashcards.",
